-- (a)(iii): the police must be told where the loss was caused, or thought to be caused, by theft
-- or by malicious acts (of anyone: the clause does not say whose).
@ref General Condition 9(a)(iii) (src:341-342)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 9 requires the police to be notified of` l MEANS
        l's `theft or a malicious act was suspected`
    OR  any (GIVEN i YIELD `any cause of the Damage to` i `is one of`
                               (LIST theft
                                   , `a malicious act of the Insured or of anyone acting for the Insured`
                                   , `a malicious act of another person`))
            (l's `the damaged items`)

-- (b): within 30 days "hoặc lâu hơn" (or longer) as the Insurer agrees in writing.
@ref General Condition 9(b) (src:343-344)
GIVEN cp IS A `The claims procedure as performed`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days allowed for the written claim under` cp MEANS
    CONSIDER cp's `a longer period agreed in writing by the Insurer, in days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 30
    WHEN JUST d  THEN IF d GREATER THAN 30 THEN d ELSE 30

-- The duties as obligations. CLOCK: DAYS from the day the Insured became aware of the incident.
-- "Ngay lập tức" (immediately) is not a number the document gives, so the rule takes it as an
-- argument; the tests supply a value and say so (fork F17).
@ref General Condition 9(a) and (b) (src:335-348)
GIVEN `the days that count as immediately` IS A NUMBER
      `the police must be notified`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days allowed for the claim`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act`
`General Condition 9: the Insured's duties` `the days that count as immediately` `the police must be notified` `the days allowed for the claim` MEANS
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         MUST  `take all necessary measures to minimise the loss and recover lost property`
         WITHIN `the days that count as immediately`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "General Condition 9(a)(i): no immediate measures to minimise the loss")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         MUST  `notify the Insurer in writing`
         WITHIN `the days that count as immediately`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "General Condition 9(a)(ii): no immediate written notice to the Insurer")
    RAND
        (IF   `the police must be notified`
         THEN (PARTY `the Insured`
               MUST  `notify the police`
               WITHIN `the days that count as immediately`
               LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "General Condition 9(a)(iii): the police were not notified immediately")
         ELSE FULFILLED)
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         MUST  `submit a written claim listing the items and amounts`
         WITHIN `the days allowed for the claim`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "General Condition 9(b)(i): no written claim within the period")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         MUST  `give particulars of other insurances`
         WITHIN `the days allowed for the claim`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "General Condition 9(b)(ii): no particulars of other insurances within the period")

-- The same duties as the facts of a performed claim record them, for the claim decision.
@ref General Condition 9 (src:334-358)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`why General Condition 9 is not met` l MEANS
    concat (LIST (`reason unless` (cp's `measures to minimise the loss were taken immediately`)
                                  "General Condition 9(a)(i): no immediate measures to minimise the loss")
               , (`reason unless` (cp's `written notice was given to the Insurer immediately`)
                                  "General Condition 9(a)(ii): no immediate written notice to the Insurer")
               , (`reason unless` (    NOT `General Condition 9 requires the police to be notified of` l
                                   OR  cp's `the police were notified immediately`)
                                  "General Condition 9(a)(iii): the police were not notified immediately")
               , (`reason unless` (CONSIDER cp's `days from awareness to the written claim`
                                   WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                                   WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT MOST `the days allowed for the written claim under` cp)
                                  "General Condition 9(b)(i): no written claim within the period")
               , (`reason unless` (cp's `particulars of other insurances were given`)
                                  "General Condition 9(b)(ii): no particulars of other insurances")
               , (`reason unless` (cp's `the information and documents the Insurer reasonably required were provided, with a declaration of truth`)
                                  "General Condition 9, last paragraph: the information and documents required were not provided"))
    WHERE
        cp MEANS l's `the Insured's conduct`'s `the claims procedure`

§§ `General Condition 10: the Insurer's rights over the property`

-- The Insurer MAY enter and take possession of the property or the premises, take or require
-- delivery of property there, keep it to examine, sort, move or deal with, and sell or dispose of
-- it, at any time until the Insured says in writing it will not claim or, if it claims, until the
-- claim is decided or withdrawn; doing so creates no liability to the Insured. Non-compliance
-- with the Insurer's requirements, or hindering it, forfeits all the Insured's benefits. The
-- Insured may never abandon property to the Insurer.
