GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period of insurance in days` s MEANS
    `the number of days in` (s's `the period of insurance`)

-- 1(a)(i): a period of insurance of 30 days or more: within 30 days from the day the cover was
-- accepted. 1(b)(i): instalments accepted: the first within 30 days of that day, the rest on the
-- agreed dates. 1(c): "khi thời hạn thanh toán phí bảo hiểm dưới 30 ngày" — fork F26 reads it as
-- a PERIOD OF INSURANCE under 30 days (the counterpart of (a); Finding 4), for which the premium
-- is due within the period itself.
@ref General Condition 15, clause 1(a)(i), (b)(i), (c) (src:418-444)
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      p IS A `The premium payment`
GIVETH A DATE
`General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` s p MEANS
    BRANCH IF p's `the Insurer accepted payment by instalments`
           THEN p's `date the cover was accepted` PLUS 30
           IF `the period of insurance in days` s AT LEAST 30
           THEN p's `date the cover was accepted` PLUS 30
           OTHERWISE s's `the period of insurance`'s `last day`

-- 1(a)(ii) and (iii): for an endorsement, 30 days from the day its cover takes effect where that
-- is on or after the day it was issued, and otherwise from the day it was issued.
@ref General Condition 15, clause 1(a)(ii)-(iii) (src:426-432)
GIVEN e IS AN `An endorsement`
GIVETH A DATE
`General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium for` e MEANS
    IF   e's `date the cover in it takes effect` AT LEAST e's `date it was issued`
    THEN e's `date the cover in it takes effect` PLUS 30
    ELSE e's `date it was issued` PLUS 30

-- Clause 2: if the premium is not paid in full within the warranty period, the cover is cancelled
-- and the Insurer is liable only for the time the documents were in force, up to the day of
-- cancellation. Fork F27: clause 1 is "phụ thuộc và không phương hại đến điều khoản số 2"
-- (subject to and without prejudice to clause 2), so a loss on or before the last day of the
-- warranty period stays covered though the premium is never paid; the cancellation takes effect
-- after that day. LAW art 27(1)(c) (aid line 652-657) agrees for property insurance ended for
-- non-payment. For an instalment missed later, the cover runs to that instalment's agreed date.
@ref General Condition 15, clause 2 (src:445-449)
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      p IS A `The premium payment`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` s p d MEANS
    IF   CONSIDER p's `date the premium was paid in full`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` s p
    THEN CONSIDER p's `agreed date of the first later instalment not paid on time`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST m  THEN d AT MOST m
    ELSE d AT MOST `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` s p

@ref General Condition 15, clause 2 (src:445-449)
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`why General Condition 15 has cancelled the cover` s l MEANS
    `reason unless` (`General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` s (l's `the premium payment`) (l's `date of the loss`))
                    "General Condition 15: the cover had been cancelled for non-payment of the premium before the loss"

§§ `The closing note`

-- "GHI CHÚ QUAN TRỌNG": the Insured must tell the Insurer truthfully and fully everything it knows
-- or could know, so as not to affect its right to indemnity. Inert: it states the duty General
-- Condition 2 sanctions and adds no consequence of its own.
-- src:452 | GHI CHÚ QUAN TRỌNG
-- src:453 | Người được bảo hiểm phải thông báo cho Người bảo hiểm một cách trung thực và đầy đủ tất cả các
-- src:454 | dữ liệu mà Người được bảo hiểm biết hoặc có thể biết để không bị ảnh hưởng đến quyền được bồi
-- src:455 | thường từ Hợp đồng bảo hiểm này

§ `The conditions the claim decision applies`

-- Forfeitures (General Conditions 4(a), 10), the premium warranty (15), and the conditions
-- precedent (5, 9, 11, 12, 13), in that order. Fork F28: a failure of any of them defeats the
-- whole claim, as "điều kiện tiên quyết" says. LAW: art 46 (aid line 917-932) allows an insurer to
-- reduce, not refuse, for late notice, and only by the loss it suffered and only where the
-- contract states that sanction; art 19(3) (aid line 441-444) bars a late-notice exclusion where
-- force majeure caused the delay. Recorded, not applied.
@ref insuring clause (src:9-11); General Conditions 4, 5, 9-13, 15
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      l IS A `A loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`why the general conditions defeat the claim` s l MEANS
    concat (LIST (`why General Condition 4(a) forfeits the benefits` l)
               , (`why General Condition 10 forfeits the benefits` l)
               , (`why General Condition 15 has cancelled the cover` s l)
               , (`why General Condition 5 is not met` l)
               , (`why General Condition 9 is not met` l)
               , (`why General Condition 11 is not met` l)
               , (`why General Condition 12 is not met` l)
               , (`why General Condition 13 is not met` l))
